@page "/theming"

<DocsHeader Title="Theming" Eyebrow="Get started">
    <Lead>Stil is themed entirely with <code>--stil-*</code> CSS custom properties. Change a few, and every component follows, in light and dark mode.</Lead>
</DocsHeader>

<p>Try it in the <a href="theme-builder">theme builder</a>, then copy the result.</p>

<h2 id="brand">Change the brand</h2>
<p>Most themes only need the brand colors. In a Blazor app, set them in <code>AddStil</code>; <code>&lt;StilHead /&gt;</code> writes them to the page:</p>
<CodeBlock Language="csharp" Code="@CSharpSnippet" />
<p>Or in CSS, after <code>stil.css</code>. Stil's rules are in cascade layers, so your CSS wins wherever it is loaded:</p>
<CodeBlock Language="css" Code="@CssSnippet" />

<p>Everything derived from a color follows it:</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Text on colored backgrounds</strong> (buttons, alerts, badges) is black or white, whichever contrasts more. That always meets WCAG AA. To force a color, set <code>--stil-color-{variant}-contrast</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Links, focus rings and selected states</strong> use the primary color, darkened in light mode and lightened in dark mode until they are readable. Set <code>--stil-color-accent</code> to use another color.</li>
    <li><strong>Outline and ghost buttons</strong> and colored text use the variant color, adjusted the same way.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="part">Theme part of a page</h2>
<p>Tokens apply to everything inside the element that sets them. <code>StilThemeProvider</code> does that for you:</p>
<DocExample Type="typeof(Examples.Theming.Provider)" ShowCode />

<h2 id="modes">Light, dark and auto</h2>
<p>
    Stil renders light unless you opt in, so it never turns a host page dark by accident. Set
    <code>data-stil-theme</code> to <code>light</code>, <code>dark</code> or <code>auto</code> (follows the
    operating system) on <code>&lt;html&gt;</code> or any element, or use <code>Mode</code> on
    <code>StilThemeProvider</code>:
</p>
<DocExample Type="typeof(Examples.Theming.Modes)" />
<p>The neutral colors are written as <code>light-dark(light, dark)</code>. Use the same form when you override them:</p>
<CodeBlock Language="css" Code="@NeutralSnippet" />

<h2 id="tokens">Tokens</h2>
<div class="stil-table-responsive">
    <table class="stil-table stil-table-compact">
        <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">Group</th><th scope="col">Tokens</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            @foreach (var (group, tokens) in Tokens)
            {
                <tr><th scope="row">@group</th><td><code class="docs-type">@tokens</code></td></tr>
            }
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>

<h2 id="fonts">Fonts</h2>
<p>
    Stil uses Lexend if your page loads it, for example from <code>https://fonts.cdnfonts.com/css/lexend</code>, and falls back to
    <code>sans-serif</code>. The stylesheet never fetches fonts itself. Set <code>--stil-font-family</code>
    (or <code>StilTheme.FontFamily</code>) to use another font.
</p>
<p>
    In Blazor, <code>options.Font</code> picks a web font for the whole app: <code>&lt;StilHead /&gt;</code> links its
    stylesheet and sets <code>--stil-font-family</code>. <code>StilFonts</code> has ready-made fonts from cdnfonts.com
    (Lexend, BR Cobane, BR Segma, BR Sonoma, BR Shape, Averral, Sukplena, and the display fonts BLOWREPH, Taster and
    Zagist). <code>StilFont.CdnFonts</code> takes any other font there by its name, and <code>StilFont.Google</code> any
    Google font. The <a href="theme-builder">theme builder</a> previews them, and <code>dotnet new stil-app</code> takes
    <code>--Font</code> and <code>--GoogleFont</code>.
</p>
<CodeBlock Language="csharp" Code="@FontSnippet" />
<p>
    The page then loads the font from that site, which sees your visitors' IP addresses. Check each font's license on
    cdnfonts.com before you use it in a product; some are free for personal use only. To host a font yourself, pass your
    own stylesheet: <code>new StilFont("My Font", "fonts/my-font.css")</code>.
</p>

@code {
    private const string FontSnippet = """
        // using Stil.Blazor;
        builder.Services.AddStil(options => options.Font = StilFonts.BrCobane);

        // Any font from cdnfonts.com, by its name (or its slug, the last part of its address there):
        options.Font = StilFont.CdnFonts("Gilroy");
        // Any Google font, in the 400 and 600 weights Stil uses:
        options.Font = StilFont.Google("Open Sans");
        """;

    private const string CSharpSnippet = """
        builder.Services.AddStil(options =>
        {
            options.Theme.Primary = "#6741d9";
            options.Theme.Secondary = "#d0bfff";
            options.Theme.FontFamily = "system-ui, sans-serif";
            options.Theme.Radius = "0.5rem";
        });
        """;

    private const string CssSnippet = """
        :root {
            --stil-color-primary: #6741d9;
            --stil-color-secondary: #d0bfff;
            --stil-font-family: system-ui, sans-serif;
            --stil-radius-md: 0.5rem;
        }
        """;

    private const string NeutralSnippet = """
        :root {
            --stil-color-surface: light-dark(#fffdf8, #1a1b1e);
        }
        """;

    private static readonly (string Group, string Tokens)[] Tokens =
    [
        ("Brand colors", "--stil-color-primary, -secondary, -success, -danger, -warning, -info"),
        ("Overrides", "--stil-color-{variant}-contrast, --stil-color-accent"),
        ("Neutrals", "--stil-color-body-bg, -surface, -surface-muted, -text, -text-muted, -border, -border-strong"),
        ("Typography", "--stil-font-family, --stil-font-family-mono, --stil-font-size-xs … -2xl, --stil-font-weight-normal, -bold, --stil-line-height, --stil-letter-spacing"),
        ("Spacing", "--stil-space-1 (0.25rem) … --stil-space-7 (3rem)"),
        ("Layout", "--stil-container-max, --stil-sidebar-width"),
        ("Shape", "--stil-radius-sm, -md, -lg, -pill, --stil-shadow-sm, -md, -lg, --stil-backdrop"),
        ("Focus", "--stil-focus-ring-width, --stil-focus-ring-offset"),
        ("Layering", "--stil-z-dropdown, -sticky, -overlay, -modal, -popover, -toast"),
        ("Motion", "--stil-duration-fast, --stil-duration-md, --stil-easing (0 ms with reduced motion)"),
    ];
}
